  "slug": "fast-radio-neural-0765",
  "summary": "Five preprints in one week apply neural posterior, map-level, transformer and generative methods to FRB, CMB, kSZ and gravitational-wave cosmology inference.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the substitution of neural, simulation-trained estimators for conventional analytic or sampling-based steps in cosmological inference. AttNPE recovers FRB cosmology posteriors matching MCMC at roughly 10^6 lower cost. A spherical graph CNN infers r directly from multifrequency B-mode maps, beating a bandpower likelihood on RMSE and intervals. Simulation-based inference reconstructs first-order electroweak phase transition parameters from stochastic gravitational-wave backgrounds. Vision Transformers outperform quadratic estimators in kSZ velocity reconstruction fidelity. Wavelet-CFM generates jointly correlated lensing, kSZ, tSZ and CIB maps, matching validation statistics. What is new is the breadth: neural methods now span posterior estimation, map-level inference, field reconstruction and simulation generation, with interpretability (AttNPE) and benchmarks against standard estimators as recurring elements.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
